Sender icon assets
==================

The sender avatar catalog contains original-color raster app artwork returned
by Apple's public iTunes Search/Lookup API and first-party touch icons/favicons
from the brands' official websites. Per-brand source metadata, including App
Store track ID, bundle ID, seller, country, fetched artwork URL, source pixel
dimensions, website URLs, license field, and guidelines URL, is stored in
Sources/Core/Resources/sender-brands.json. Ninety-three entries use App Store
artwork, seven use first-party website icons, and twelve use generated initial
monograms because no qualifying official raster icon was verified.

The `license: "none"` value means the source did not provide a per-image SPDX
license identifier. It does not grant reproduction rights or put an image in
the public domain. The images, brand names, and marks remain the property of
their respective owners. They are bundled only to identify the source of an
email sender and do not indicate authentication, sponsorship, affiliation, or
endorsement.

Every brand record defaults to `publicReleaseReviewed: false`. Review the
trademark use and source terms for each individual mark before public release;
the catalog validator lists all records that still require that review.
